62	WorkPackage	45	4	**Batch determination — municipal witness-test waiver batch (record as it stands at 07/14/2025)**\n\nPackage filed: /DER_Program/Commissioning/Municipal/Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx\n\n**Scope on 07/14/2025:** five arrays in scope — Cravenwood High, Darnwick Elementary, Holcott Public Library, Lockmere Middle, Marden Falls WRF. Tresbay Community Center is out of the batch (withdrew its request 07/09/2025): no carriage call, no scheduling item, not on the release list.\n\n**CEL edition:** CEL-2025-Q2 (eff. 04/30/2025; supersedes CEL-2024-Q4). No later edition published as of 07/14/2025. CEL-2025-Q3 is planned for 07/31/2025 — any waiver signed after Q3 takes effect needs the lookup redone (ENG-PRC-014 §3 corollaries 1 and 5).\n\n**Carriage calls — equipment actually installed (ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3 §3, §4.1):**\n\n| Array | Installed inverter | CEL-2025-Q2 body | Call |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Cravenwood High | Solmery SM-215K-3P | Inverters row 6 | **CARRIED** — waiver eligible; to Standards Engineering for written disposition |\n| Darnwick Elementary | Arvexa PV-750 | not listed | **NOT CARRIED** — on-site witness test required before PTO |\n| Holcott Public Library | Selvix SV-720 | not listed (superseded CEL-2024-Q4 only) | **NOT CARRIED** — witness test required |\n| Lockmere Middle | Selvix SV-720 — substituted on site after the checklist was submitted (Standards Engineering file note on the commissioning wiki); checklist still shows 4 × Torvane TE-180K | not listed | **NOT CARRIED** — witness test required |\n| Marden Falls WRF | 4 × Solmery SM-245K-3P | Inverters row 7 | **CARRIED** — waiver eligible; to Standards Engineering for written disposition |\n\nThe copy-forward "waiver eligible" pre-marks on all six checklists were not relied on. No waiver disposition is made here; it remains with Standards Engineering.\n\n**Witness tests** (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, per IEEE 1547.1, minimum: protective-function trip tests, anti-islanding test, ride-through verifications; performed by the customer or its commissioning agent with its test plan, calibrated instruments and qualified operators; witnessed, recorded and dispositioned by an Alleniom Utilities witness engineer): Darnwick (#47), Holcott (#48), Lockmere (#49).\n\n**SOC release list as the record stands:** Marden Falls WRF only — once Standards Engineering signs its waiver disposition, with the SOC confirming live telemetry at the moment PTO is requested (TCS-02 §5). Not releasable: Cravenwood (RTU/telemetry pending), Lockmere (witness test outstanding, although telemetry is live), Darnwick and Holcott (witness test and telemetry). No array held a signed waiver or witness-test disposition on 07/14/2025.\n\n**Reconciliation:** arrays named in the package for witness test = {Darnwick, Holcott, Lockmere}; scheduling items standing on this case = {#47 Darnwick, #48 Holcott, #49 Lockmere}; none for Cravenwood, Marden Falls or Tresbay. The two sets agree, so the case is closed. The three scheduling items stay open until the tests are held and the signed records are on file.\n\n**Flagged to Standards Engineering (not dispositioned):** (1) the ENG-PRC-014 §4.2 cross-reference to DIS-01 Rev 4 §6 points to Monitoring and Control, which has no test specifications; (2) protective-device listing under §3 corollary 2 — no relay make/model on the checklists, and no protective-device listings on CEL-2025-Q2; (3) Lockmere needs a checklist revision, an ISA change order (DIS-01 §7) and per-block telemetry re-verification (TCS-02 §6.1); (4) the Darnwick protection basis under DIS-01 Table 5-1 Cat. 2 needs confirming; (5) the Marden Falls checklist misstates the §3 waiver-date rule.	2026-11-24 22:32:36.097991+00	2	2026-11-24 22:32:44.876639+00	Journal::WorkPackageJournal	116	{}	["2026-11-24 22:32:36.097991+00",)	f
